<blockquote class="uncited"><div>the minimum audio level, just above the 'off' level, is higher than I would like.</div></blockquote>Unfortunately this is basically a hardware limitation.<br><br>If its DMR you are listening to, sometimes the received audio data has very high intrinsic volume levels. In which case you could try turing on the DMR AGC setting and turn down the AGC gain, but this will have the effect of making all DMR signals less loud and also have the AGC turned on, which will attempt to normalise the volume on all signals , not just loud signals<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Jul 09, 2025 8:32 pm</p><hr />
